# Shell scripts must keep UNIX line endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# This matters concretely here: the Veeam pre-freeze/post-thaw scripts are
# stored on a Windows backup server, and Git's autocrlf would rewrite them to
# CRLF on checkout. Veeam then uploads them to the Linux agent, where the
# shebang fails with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" and the backup job aborts.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else consumed by Linux.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
